<title>USA: Tiffany &amp; Co says plans selective expansion.</title>
<headline>Tiffany &amp; Co says plans selective expansion.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tiffany &amp; Co said Wednesday its plans for the year call for selective store expansion into four United States markets, Japan and several other Asian-Pacific locations.</p>
<p>The company said its plans for the U.S. include new stores in Palo Alto, Calif. and Cincinnati, Ohio.</p>
<p>The company also said it is finalizing plans in Latin America to open its first Tiffany &amp; Co boutique in Mexico City.</p>
<p>The company reported earnings for the first quarter of $8.88 million, or $0.25 per share, compared to earnings of $5.08 cents a share for the same period a year ago.</p>
</text>
